  "id": "b6d31a09-77ba-4044-8317-a6877470ef6b",
  "title": "Dynamic Modality Knockout and Modality Synthesis for Multimodal Learning",
  "summary": "ShapKO improves robustness by dynamically learning modality-specific knockout probabilities, while VVM-Tuning enables zero-shot adaptation to unseen modalities through synthetic modality synthesis. Both methods address modality dominance and partial availability issues.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "ShapKO introduces a dynamic training strategy that learns modality-specific knockout probabilities based on validation utility.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "VVM-Tuning uses modality synthesis to disentangle invariant semantics from varying visual appearances and enables zero-shot adaptation to unseen modalities.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both methods demonstrate improved performance on real-world and synthetic modalities without requiring architectural modifications.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
